  "question": {
    "text": "A sphere of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> is projected in a gravity free space with speed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. If the coefficient of viscosity of the medium in which it moves is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Pa</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> , the distance travelled by the body before it stops is :",
